Analyze this {language} code for KISS (Keep It Simple) violations and over-engineering.

Source file:
{source}

Return a JSON array of violations:
{{
  "pattern": "over-abstraction|premature-generalization|unnecessary-pattern|complex-solution|speculative-design",
  "line": <line number>,
  "severity": "high|medium|low",
  "violation": "what makes this unnecessarily complex",
  "suggestion": "simpler alternative"
}}

Look for: abstract factories for a single implementation, strategy pattern when a simple if suffices,
generic type parameters that are never varied, visitor pattern on 2 types,
builder pattern for 2-field objects, over-parameterized functions.

Return [] if no violations. Return ONLY the JSON array.
